1.FIRST DIGIT OF A NUMBER 
Given a number n, find the first digit of the number.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public static int firstDigit(int n) {
                while(n>=10){
                    n/=10;
                }
                return n;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/first-digit-of-a-number/1


2.ALL DIVISORS OF A NUMBER 
Given an integer n, return all the divisors of n in the ascending order.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public ArrayList<Integer> getDivisors(int n) {
                ArrayList<Integer> list=new ArrayList<>();
                for(int i=1;i*i<=n;i++){
                    if(n%i==0){
                        list.add(i);
                        if(i!=n/i){
                            list.add(n/i);
                        }
                    }
                }
                Collections.sort(list);
                return list;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/all-divisors-of-a-number/1


3.FACTORIALS LESS THAN OR EQUAL TO N 
A number n is called a factorial number if it is the factorial of a positive integer. For example, the first few factorial numbers are 1, 2, 6, 24, 120,
Given a number n, the task is to return the list/vector of the factorial numbers smaller than or equal to n.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            static ArrayList<Long> factorialNumbers(long n) {
                ArrayList<Long> list=new ArrayList<>();
                long fact=1;
                for(int i=1;;i++){
                    fact*=i;
                    if(fact>n){
                        break;
                    }
                    list.add(fact);
                }
                return list;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/find-all-factorial-numbers-less-than-or-equal-to-n3548/1?problemType=functional&query=problemTypefunctionaldifficulty%5B%5D-1page1&page=1&difficulty%5B%5D=-1


4.NTH TERM OF GP FROM FIRST TWO TERMS 
Given the first 2 terms a and b of a Geometric Series. The task is to find the nth term of the series.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public int termOfGP(int a, int b, int n) {
                double r=(double)b/a;
                return (int) (a*Math.pow(r,n-1));
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/gp-term/1


5.MEAN AND MEDIAN OF ARRAY 
Given an array of positive integer arr[]. Find the mean and median of the array. 
Where mean is the average value of the given array, median is the average of the two middle elements.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public int mean(int[] arr) {
                int sum=0;
                for(int num:arr){
                    sum+=num;
                }
                return sum/arr.length;
            }
            public int median(int[] arr) {
                Arrays.sort(arr);
                if(arr.length%2!=0){
                    return arr[arr.length/2];
                }
                else{
                    return (arr[(arr.length/2)-1]+arr[arr.length/2])/2;
                }
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/mean-and-median-1587115620/1


6.TWO REPEATED ELEMENTS 
You are given an integer array arr of size n+2. All elements of the array are in the range from 1 to n. Also, all elements occur once except two numbers which occur twice. Find the two repeating numbers.
Note: Return the numbers in their order of appearing twice. So, if x and y are repeating numbers, and x's second appearance comes before the second appearance of y, then the order should be (x, y).
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public int[] twoRepeated(int[] arr) {
                HashMap<Integer,Integer> map=new HashMap<>();
                int res[]=new int[2];
                int count=0;
                for(int num:arr){
                    map.put(num, map.getOrDefault(num,0)+1);
                    if(map.get(num)==2){
                        res[count++]=num;
                    }
                }
                return res;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/two-repeated-elements-1587115621/1


7.STOCK BUY AND SELL-MAX ONE TRANSACTION ALLOWED 
Given an array prices[] of non-negative integers, representing the prices of the stocks on different days. 
The task is to find the maximum profit possible by buying and selling the stocks on different days when at most one transaction is allowed. 
Here one transaction means 1 buy + 1 Sell. If it is not possible to make a profit then return 0.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public int maxProfit(int[] prices) {
                int minPrice=prices[0];
                int maxPrice=0;
                for(int stock:prices){
                    int profit=stock-minPrice;
                    minPrice=Math.min(stock,minPrice);
                    maxPrice=Math.max(profit,maxPrice);
                }
                return maxPrice;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/buy-stock-2/1
